// A contract a service consumes (compiled with FORWARDS_SESSION), so its slots carry the
// session and the trace the calling entity is acting in. The shape of the second hop of
// a click, where the trace has to be continued rather than started.
contract Ledger {
    slot post(string[32] item)

    // Gated, so the second hop has a way to refuse. A refusal is the one thing a monitor
    // keeps when ordinary calls are turned down, which is what makes it the case that has
    // to stay joined to the click that caused it.
    <moderator> slot audit(string[32] item)
}
